# Pages and breaks: Before: page starts a box on a new page.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Pages and breaks · Break before
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Page overlay:
		Offset: auto 0 -24 0
		Text: Page {page} of {pages}
			Typography:
				Align: right
	Section:
		Text: Pages and breaks
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Break before
		Paragraph: With `Before: page` in its `Break`, a box starts on a new page even when there is room left on the current one. The second block below declares it and opens page 2.
			Style: intro
		Block:
			Style: marked
			Text: Break: (none)
				Style: label
			Paragraph: This block follows the explanation on the first page, as usual.
		Block:
			Style: marked
			Break:
				Before: page
			Text: Break: Before: page
				Style: label
			Paragraph: This block starts at the top of page 2, although page 1 had room for it.
